  "id": "steinerts-disease",
  "term": "Steinert’s disease",
  "definition": "Steinert’s disease is a neuromuscular condition involving ongoing loss of muscle tissue, delayed muscle relaxation, and wasting that can affect multiple body systems. Some people may also have mild intellectual disability, and the disorder is linked to repeat expansions in genes associated with myotonic dystrophy types 1 and 2.",
